@page "/data-dictionary"
@layout MarketingLayout
@using Brainy.Application.Analytics

<HeadContent>
    <SeoHeadContent Path="/data-dictionary"
                    Title="Analytics Data Dictionary — Brainy"
                    Description="Every internal product-analytics event Brainy records, its purpose, retention period, and whether it is optional." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="mkt-hero">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <span class="mkt-eyebrow mkt-rise">Trust</span>
        <h1 class="mkt-title mkt-rise mkt-d1" style="max-width: 20em; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);">
            Analytics data dictionary
        </h1>
        <p class="mkt-lead mkt-rise mkt-d2" style="margin-top: 1.1rem;">
            Every internal product-analytics event Brainy records, why, for how long, and whether you can opt out.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <article class="mkt-changelog">
            <h2>What this page is</h2>
            <p>
                Brainy measures whether its core workflow helps people capture, organize, and retrieve
                knowledge &mdash; not how long they stay on the page. This page lists every event the product
                can record for that purpose. Content-level telemetry would conflict with Brainy's trust
                proposition, so it is explicitly out of bounds:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Note, task, output, and other item <strong>content is never recorded</strong>.</li>
                <li>Search query text is never recorded, only that a search happened and whether it matched.</li>
                <li>AI prompts and AI-generated text are never recorded, only request/outcome counts.</li>
                <li>Every event is tied to your account so it can be exported or deleted with your data, but it
                    is never shared with an external analytics vendor.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Your control</h2>
            <p>
                Analytics tracking defaults to on, with this page linked from the toggle. You can turn it off at
                any time from <a href="/Account/Manage">Account and data</a>; turning it off stops
                all future event recording for your account immediately. Your recorded events are included in
                your data export and deleted with your account, the same as everything else you own.
            </p>

            <h2>Events</h2>
            <div class="mkt-table-wrap" style="overflow-x: auto;">
                <table class="mkt-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Event name</th>
                            <th>Purpose</th>
                            <th>Retention</th>
                            <th>Optional</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        @foreach (var descriptor in AnalyticsEvents.All)
                        {
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>@descriptor.EventName</code></td>
                                <td>@descriptor.Purpose</td>
                                <td>@descriptor.RetentionPeriod</td>
                                <td>@(descriptor.IsOptional ? "Yes" : "No")</td>
                            </tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .mkt-table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.92rem;
    }

    .mkt-table th,
    .mkt-table td {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mud-palette-lines-default);
        vertical-align: top;
    }

    .mkt-table th {
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
    }
</style>
